      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly, here's a professional overview for the High-Rise Fire/Evacuation protocol:\n\n---\n\n**High-Rise Fire/Evacuation Protocol: Brief Overview**\n\nDuring a high-rise fire scenario, the following steps will be initiated by our dispatch team and operators:\n\n1. Immediate notification to the on-duty fire brigade and building management.\n2. Activation of the building's internal alarm system to alert all occupants.\n3. Immediate commencement of evacuation protocols per Life Safety Codes 101, including clear signage to exits, and coordination with ADA-compliant routes.\n4. Dispatch of Fire Brigade to establish command post and commence fire suppression efforts.\n5. Real-time coordination with local EMS for potential emergencies.\n6. Immediate liaison with law enforcement for crowd control and confirmation of all evacuees.\n\nUpon receiving a fire emergency, all frontline operational staff are to ensure adherence to these procedures while maintaining clear communication with command units. Safety and prompt action remain paramount.\n\n---\n\nMake sure this communication is received and acknowledged by all your field units, and they'll be flagged as 'critical' by the system accordingly. Let me know if there's anything more you need!",
